  "classification_notes": [
    "The homepage highlights three AI directions in this order: AI for Software Engineering, Trustworthy LLMs & Agents, and AI for Web3.",
    "Research Foundations is a supporting archive, not a fourth peer direction. It includes ongoing as well as earlier work in Web3 security, ecosystem measurement, software quality, and systems.",
    "Each paper has one category and cross-cutting tags. The three AI directions contain 20, 7, and 17 papers; foundations contains 56, totaling 100 without duplication.",
    "AI for Web3 includes contract-specific AI/LLM/learning methods, even when security is the application. General development capabilities belong to AI for Software Engineering; security and reliability of models and agents belong to Trustworthy LLMs & Agents.",
    "Foundation papers retain their original subfield in foundation_area. They are not relabeled as AI work solely to match the new homepage emphasis.",
    "AI for Web3 includes early ML/GNN work. An automated tool, dataset, or non-LLM collaborative agent is not treated as an LLM contribution without evidence.",
    "Assignment is interpretive and based mainly on titles, with selected ambiguous methods checked against primary sources. Original bibliographic metadata is preserved.",
    "Agentic Economy and Web3 for AI remain stated broader interests, not additional publication-backed primary categories."
